  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the price of a movie ticket on the last Friday? Colby's parents give him $155 each month to spend at the movies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The information given is not enough to determine the ticket price. The $155 is Colby’s **total monthly movie budget**, but we are not told how many tickets he buys or how much he spends on other items.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The price of the ticket on the last Friday cannot be determined from the given information.}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Colby's parents give him $150 each month to spend at the movies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Even if Colby’s parents give him **$150 per month**, that only tells us his total monthly movie budget. We still need information such as how many movies he attends or whether he spends money on other things.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The movie ticket price on the last Friday cannot be determined.}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Tickets for movies on Fridays and Saturdays cost $11, while tickets on all other days cost $7.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. The last Friday is a **Friday**.\n2. Friday movie tickets cost **$11**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$11}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Tickets for movies on Fridays and Saturdays cost $10, while tickets on all other days cost $7.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The last Friday is a Friday, and Friday tickets cost $10.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: the last Friday is a regular Friday, not a holiday or special event.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since the last Friday is a regular Friday, the Friday ticket price applies:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Colby buys his ticket at the standard box-office price.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Colby buys the ticket at the standard box-office price, and a regular Friday ticket costs $10.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How many additional movies can Colby see on the last Friday while staying within his monthly movie budget? By the way, here are some relevant details: A tub of popcorn costs $8, and a box of candy costs $2. Colby has already seen 5 movies on Fridays or Saturdays and 8 movies on other days during the month. Colby has already had 2 tubs of popcorn and 4 boxes of candy during the month, and he wants one tub of popcorn and one box of candy on the last Friday.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Calculate Colby’s spending so far:\n\n- Friday/Saturday movies: \\(5 \\times \\$10 = \\$50\\)\n- Other movies: \\(8 \\times \\$7 = \\$56\\)\n- Popcorn: \\(2 \\times \\$8 = \\$16\\)\n- Candy: \\(4 \\times \\$2 = \\$8\\)\n\nTotal spent:\n\n\\[\n50+56+16+8=\\$130\n\\]\n\nHis remaining budget is:\n\n\\[\n\\$150-\\$130=\\$20\n\\]\n\nOn the last Friday, he plans to buy:\n\n- Popcorn: \\(\\$8\\)\n- Candy: \\(\\$2\\)\n\nSo, he has:\n\n\\[\n\\$20-(\\$8+\\$2)=\\$10\n\\]\n\nleft for movie tickets. Since each Friday ticket costs \\(\\$10\\),\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$10}{\\$10}=1\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1\\text{ additional movie}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
